  "notes": "Guitar-and-string melodic trap written fast — the research documents a flagship record built in about fifteen minutes, and low layer counts are the parameter that follows from it. Three things carry the model: a nylon-guitar lead in `melody.timbreHint` over a genuinely tonal i–VI–III–VII bed, an 808 with the longest portamento on this bench (`glideProb` 0.75, `portamentoMs` up to 220) sliding between chord roots, and the sparsest fill schedule the band allows. The tempo floor is unusually low for trap because the research says his signature record sits there. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this high-medium. ⚠ INFERRED: `drums.kick.avoidPreSnareGap` is set to `16th` rather than the genre's `8th` — that is my reading of \"kick with a 16th pickup into 3\", and it is the one parameter here that is a translation rather than a quotation. The bpm `mode` of 132 is also inferred; the research gives bounds, not a centre.",
